## 1. Purpose

The main paper has a single positive control (E71) showing that
FedPer + task-specific calibration is statistically indistinguishable
from the full PC²-FedReorg architecture on the C-triplet target. This
study tests whether that effect generalises beyond the C-triplet
sample.

## 2. Why this does NOT change main-paper C-hole / C-triplet results

- All experiments use the public QM9-derived `public_reorg_energy_15210.csv`
  with synthetic label transforms (Phase 1) or label-quantile-binned
  splits (Phase 2). The TADF private data (`results/e71_*`, C-hole, C-triplet)
  is untouched.
- No existing `results/*.csv` or `results/*.json` is overwritten.
- No `src/` or `experiments/run_all.py` file is modified.

